--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

LoadForge has NO third-party runtime dependencies. The shipped binary links only
against libc and libstdc++ (and, in the static build, not even those
dynamically). Components below are build- or test-time only and are never linked
into the released executable.

  GoogleTest / GoogleMock
    Role     : test framework (test-only, not linked into the binary)
    Licence  : BSD-3-Clause  -- GPL-compatible
    Version  : v1.15.2, pinned by commit SHA in cmake/Dependencies.cmake
               (LOADFORGE_GTEST_SHA). A tag is a movable reference; the SHA is not.
    Source   : https://github.com/google/googletest
    Obtained : system package where available, otherwise FetchContent at the
               pinned SHA. Skipped entirely with -DLOADFORGE_BUILD_TESTS=OFF,
               so an offline or live-media build needs no network.

  gcovr
    Role     : coverage measurement and the 100% gate (CI only)
    Licence  : BSD-3-Clause  -- GPL-compatible

  mull
    Role     : mutation testing (CI only, on demand -- not yet scheduled,
               pending a release pinned by verified SHA-256)
    Licence  : Apache-2.0  -- GPL-compatible

No component is vendored under third_party/ yet.

third_party/MANIFEST.toml is the authoritative record: name, version, immutable
SHA, source, licence and whether it is linked into the binary. CI
(tools/check-dependencies.py) validates every licence against a GPL-compatible
allowlist, requires a full 40-character SHA for fetched components, rejects
anything vendored but undeclared, and checks that the SHA in the manifest is the
SHA the build actually pins. This file is prose for humans; the manifest is what
CI enforces.
